038t36y30"}], "full_name": "Joos, E.", "last_name": "Joos", "first_name": "E.", "recid": 2282855}, "control_number": 199214, "dois": [{"value": "10.1007/BF01725541"}], "earliest_date": "1984-12", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Joos:1984uk"], "abstracts": [{"source": "Springer", "value": "The dependence of macroscopic systems upon their environment is studied under the assumption that quantum theory is universally valid. In particular scattering of photons and molecules turns out to be essential even in intergalactic space in restricting the observable properties by locally destroying the corresponding phase relations. The remaining coherence determines the ‘classical’ properties of the macroscopic systems. In this way local classical properties have their origin in the nonlocal character of quantum states.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "Springer"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"title": "The Emergence of classical properties through interaction with the environment"}], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-661074"}], "facet_author_name": ["2282855_Erich Joos", "982291_H.Dieter Zeh"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:199214", "updated": "2023-03-09T22:14:50.858620"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Z.Phys.B", "Z. Phys. B"]}, "created": "1997-05-06T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-09T22:14:50.858620+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1007%2Fbf01725541&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1007%2Fbf01725541&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1007%2Fbf01725541&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1007%2Fbf01725541&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1007%2Fbf01725541&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": 